 class=\"bullet\">Click on the incorrect word.</span> \n<span class=\"bullet\">Type in the correct word to complete the sentence.\n</span> <span class=\"bullet\">Use capital letters where necessary.</span>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}]}], "id": 9, "stimuli_ids": []}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "RSLT", "questions": [{"responses": [{"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "id": 0, "correct": 0, "selected": 0}, {"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "id": 1, "correct": 1, "selected": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": []}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Quiz", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}], "id": 10, "stimuli_ids": []}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "DWS", "questions": [{"responses": [{"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "id": 0, "correct": 1, "selected": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "engenn11le12ob09re7pdf01.pdf", "type": "pdf"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " Do a travel survey.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Take Away", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 11, "stimuli_ids": []}], "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "video", "id": 2, "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "video", "value": {"video_src": "engenn11le12ob09re2vid01", "images": [{"image": "", "text": "<span class=strong>Kristi</span>: Hey Adam! Welcome back, how was the conference? <br>\n<span class=strong>Adam</span>: It was amusing, to say the least, and rather eventful. If only I didn't have to go with Boris, it would have been better. <br>\n<span class=strong>Kristi</span>:  Why do you say that?<br>\n<span class=strong>Boris</span>: It might have been more enjoyable if you weren't pretending to be me.<br>\n<span class=strong>Kristi</span>: Adam was pretending to be you? <br>\n<span class=strong>Adam</span>: It was all a big misunderstanding. It could have been avoided had Boris been more organized.<br>\n<span class=strong>Boris</span>: Or perhaps, you could be more vigilant next time. This whole thing could have been prevented. <br>\n<span class=strong>Adam</span>: I'm just going to leave now. I'll come back later. <br>\n<span class=strong>Denise</span>: What's going on? Adam, where are you off to?<br>\n<span class=strong>Kristi</span>: They're just bickering ... like usual.", "id": 0, "time": "1"}, {"image": "", "text": "<span class=strong>Denise</span>: Gentlemen, I'm going to grab something from the boardroom. By the time I get back, I hope this bickering will have stopped. <br>\n<span class=strong>Kristi</span>: You'll have to go the boardroom a few times before that happens. <br>\n<span class=strong>Boris</span>: Denise, it was going well until we arrived at the hotel. <br>\n<span class=strong>Kristi</span>: Then what happened?<br>\n<span class=strong>Boris</span>: It just went downhill from there. <br>\n<span class=strong>Adam</span>: You could have told me about the reservation. <br>\n<span class=strong>Denise</span>: What about the reservation? I thought you had taken care of that before you left, Boris.<br>\n<span class=strong>Boris </span>: So had I, but it wasn't. I should have double-checked with my assistant. I was under the assumption reservations had been made, but unfortunately when we arrived at the hotel, they told us there was no reservation under either of our names!", "id": 1, "time": "40200"}, {"image": "", "text": "<span class=strong>Adam</span>: Ah, the embarrassment! I was mortified! How could you have forgotten to do that, Boris? Such a simple thing ... <br>\n<span class=strong>Boris</span>: Oh, Adam ... that was nothing in comparison to your run-in with Martina as we were leaving. <br>\n<span class=strong>Denise and Kristi</span>: Martina? <br>\n<span class=strong>Kristi</span>: Who's that, Adam?<br>\n<span class=strong>Boris</span>: He will not tell you. Let's just say, there was a lot of confusion. She was baffled!<br>\n<span class=strong>Adam</span>: I'd rather not comment on that. Things could have been completely different if Boris had been more organized!", "id": 2, "time": "79750"}]}}], "_data": []}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Problems and Solutions", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Misadventures at the Conference", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 9, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 12, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe the reasons or results of events or actions in spoken or written texts, in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn11le12ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " The Future Perfect Tense and the Present Perfect Tense: Review", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Future Perfect tense to say that something will be ended, completed or achieved by a particular point in the future. <br/>You use the Present Perfect tense to show a connection between a past event and a present situation.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The form of the Future Perfect tense is:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "subject + will + have + past participle", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Let's hope the rain <span class=\"strong\">will have stopped</span> by the time we land.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In this example, you hope that when you land, the rain will be finished. Using the Future Perfect tense is like you are looking back in the past from a future point.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use other modal verbs to talk about the future in a less certain way. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">By the time you get home, I <span class=\"strong\">may have already cleaned</span> the house.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The form of the Present Perfect is:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "subject + have + past participle", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">The reservations have been made. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Refer to the chart for a summary of some other commonly used tenses:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Use/Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Present Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to tell a story - it makes the action seem more direct (as if it is happening right now)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'<span class=\\\"strong\\\">m standing </span>in line at the grocery store and I realize that I forgot my wallet!</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to talk about what people have arranged to do\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Tom <span class=\\\"strong\\\">is going to the airport this afternoon</span>.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to talk about what is happening at the time of speaking\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I<span class=\\\"strong\\\">'m just calling </span>him now to see if he is free.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "By the time I get back, I hope this bickering will have stopped.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I will have gone to the boardroom several times by the time that happens.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Perfect Modals", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use Perfect modals to refer to different possibilities in the past, present and future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use a Perfect modal:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "1.  from a point of time in the past", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">We were worried. Someone <span class=\"strong\">might have taken</span> the car</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "2.  to refer back from the present", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">It is nearly eight o'clock. They will have arrived by now.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "3. to refer back from the future", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">We won't eat until they arrive. They <span class=\"strong\">might not have had</span> lunch.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "4. to refer to past time", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">could have helped</span> her when she asked.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "It might have been more enjoyable, if you weren't pretending to be me.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You could have told me about the reservation. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "How could you have forgotten to do that, Boris?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Note: You can use <span class=\"italic\"> could have (been)</span> to say that it was possible that something happened in the past (but you are not 100% sure).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"> It <span class=\"strong\">could have been avoided had</span> Boris been more organized</span>. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "amusing", "type": "name"}, {"content": "entertaining", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It was amusing to say the least and rather eventful.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le12ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to recap a business trip.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "enjoyable", "type": "name"}, {"content": "fun, giving joy, satisfying, or an event or experience that gives you pleasure", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It might have been more enjoyable, if you weren't pretending to be me.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le12ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "vigilant", "type": "name"}, {"content": "careful and observant", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Perhaps you could be more vigilant next time. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le12ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to bicker", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to argue", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They're just bickering \u2026 like usual. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le12ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to go downhill", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to decline or fail", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It just went downhill from there. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le12ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "mortified", "type": "name"}, {"content": "horrified or embarrassed", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Ah, the embarrassment! I was mortified! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le12ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "baffled", "type": "name"}, {"content": "confused", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Let's just say, there was a lot of confusion and she was baffled!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le12ob09aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Create a ten-question survey for your classmates about their travel experiences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Include questions about countries visited, best and worst foods, best and worst hotels, etc.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Tally the results of your survey into a chart.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a paragraph to present the results of your survey.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your findings with the class.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I create a travel survey.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I ask my classmates about travel experiences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I tally the results of my survey.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I compose the results into a paragraph.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I present the results to my classmates.", "type": "text"}]}]}